From: steinmarder W11 cs-observer track
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] drm/radeon: wire cs_ioctl_entry observer hook

Wires the cs_ioctl_entry observer hook.  Inserts a call to
radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_cs_ioctl_entry(data) at the prologue
of radeon_cs_ioctl, right after the body-open brace.  At this hook
point the DRM dispatcher has already copy_from_user'd the fixed-size
drm_radeon_cs args, so `data` is a kernel-side struct; the
chunks-array it points at remains in user memory and is handled by
the ib_chunk_pre_parse hook.

Adds the corresponding `#include "radeon_palm_cs_observer.h"` to
radeon_cs.c (only consumer of the hook from this TU).

Stub body in radeon_palm_cs_observer.c emits one cs_ioctl_entry
JSONL row per CS submission when the observer is enabled + the
calling task matches palm_cs_observer_comm + the per-pid event
cap is not exceeded.  Schema (one JSON object per line):

    {
        "event": "cs_ioctl_entry",
        "ts_nsec": <ktime_get_ns>,
        "pid": <current->pid>,
        "tgid": <current->tgid>,
        "comm": "<current->comm>",
        "cs_id": <user-supplied>,
        "num_chunks": <user-supplied>,
        "gart_limit_bytes": <user-supplied>,
        "vram_limit_bytes": <user-supplied>
    }

Body shorts-circuit on should_emit() returning false: disabled,
comm-mismatched, or pid-cap-exceeded.  Stack-allocated 256-byte
formatting buffer keeps the emit path allocation-free in the
critical section.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.7)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "radeon_reg.h"
 #include "radeon.h"
+#include "radeon_palm_cs_observer.h"
 #include "radeon_trace.h"

 #define RADEON_CS_MAX_PRIORITY      32u
@@ -300,6 +301,8 @@
 int radeon_cs_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
                     struct drm_file *filp)
 {
+	radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_cs_ioctl_entry(data);
+
 	struct radeon_device *rdev = dev->dev_private;
 	struct radeon_cs_parser parser;
 	int r;
